From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:15:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: psci-domain: accept OSI-only firmware on MSM8996

The PSCI firmware on MSM8996 devices (seen on the Samsung Galaxy Tab S3)
runs in OS-initiated mode from boot but does not implement
SET_SUSPEND_MODE: it answers NOT_SUPPORTED for both PC and OSI, while
PSCI_FEATURES(CPU_SUSPEND) reports OSI support. Composite StateIDs behave
as OSI requires: L2 GDHS (0x01000034) and system retention (0x02002334)
are granted to the last running CPU of a cluster or of the system and
DENIED otherwise.

psci_cpuidle_domain_probe() treats the failed mode switch as fatal and
removes the CPU PM domains, after which cpuidle-psci cannot attach the
CPUs and no idle states are left at all. On msm8996/apq8096 machines,
take NOT_SUPPORTED from the OSI switch to mean the firmware is in OSI mode
already.

With a CPU -> cluster -> system domain hierarchy this brings the Tab S3's
idle power from about 200 mA (WFI only) or 174 mA (CPU state only) down
to about 135 mA at 4.3 V.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c
index b9e4ad7d43..0b9e807c24 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/cpu.h>
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/pm_domain.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
@@ -127,6 +128,31 @@ static const struct of_device_id psci_of_match[] = {
 	{}
 };
 
+/*
+ * MSM8996 firmware runs in OS-initiated mode from boot and does not implement
+ * SET_SUSPEND_MODE: it answers NOT_SUPPORTED for both modes, while
+ * PSCI_FEATURES reports OSI support and composite cluster StateIDs get DENIED
+ * unless the caller is the last running CPU of the cluster.
+ */
+static const char *const psci_osi_only_machines[] = {
+	"qcom,apq8096",
+	"qcom,msm8996",
+	NULL
+};
+
+static int psci_cpuidle_domain_set_osi_mode(bool use_osi)
+{
+	int ret = psci_set_osi_mode(use_osi);
+
+	if (ret == -EOPNOTSUPP && use_osi &&
+	    of_machine_compatible_match(psci_osi_only_machines)) {
+		pr_info("firmware is in OSI mode already\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 static int psci_cpuidle_domain_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device_node *np = pdev->dev.of_node;
@@ -161,7 +187,7 @@ static int psci_cpuidle_domain_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		goto remove_pd;
 
 	/* let's try to enable OSI. */
-	ret = psci_set_osi_mode(use_osi);
+	ret = psci_cpuidle_domain_set_osi_mode(use_osi);
 	if (ret)
 		goto remove_pd;
 
